#callout("labquestion", title: [Question 1 --- Prepare the component stock])[For a five-bike example, receive at least 5 Aluminium Frames, 10 Rubber Tires, 5 Brake Sets, 5 Gear Sets and 5 Bicycle Chains. Record on-hand quantities before manufacturing.] #callout("labanswer", title: [Worked answer])[#strong[Inspect the result.] Each component is available in the production warehouse. A confirmed purchase order without a completed receipt is insufficient.]

#callout("labquestion", title: [Question 2 --- Create and complete the manufacturing order])[Open Manufacturing, Operations, Manufacturing Orders, then New. Select Road Bike, quantity 5 and the one-bike BOM. Confirm; inspect component quantities; record the actual consumption and produced quantity, then complete the order.] #callout("labanswer", title: [Worked answer])[#strong[Inspect the result.] The order is Done. Compare each component stock delta with the BOM multiplied by five; Road Bike stock increases by five.]

#callout("labquestion", title: [Question 3 --- Handle a shortage deliberately])[If a component is unavailable, open its product and receipt records to locate the missing quantity. Complete the receipt or correct the plan before recording production.] #callout("labanswer", title: [Worked answer])[#strong[Inspect the result.] Document the shortage and the upstream record that resolved it. Do not change the BOM merely to conceal unavailable material.]
